-- title:
--   Local lattice index at a division place of the twisted commutant
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $[L:K]=2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$, and let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$. Let $\kappa$ be a finite index type with exactly four elements and $x : \kappa \to M_2(L)$ a family that is linearly independent over $K$ and such that, for all $X \in M_2(L)$, the relation $X\delta_0 = \delta_0\, \sigma(X)$ (entrywise application of $\sigma$) holds precisely when $X$ lies in the $K$-span of the range of $x$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the completion and $\mathcal{O}_v$ for its valuation subring, and put $E_v = L \otimes_K K_v$. Write $D_v =$ `twistedCommutant K L (v.adicCompletion K) σ δ` for the $K$-subalgebra of $M_2(E_v)$ consisting of those $X$ with $X\delta = \delta\, X^{(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})}$, where $\delta$ is the image of $\delta_0$ under $L \to E_v$, $l \mapsto l \otimes 1$. Assume every non-zero element of $D_v$ is invertible in $M_2(E_v)$. Let $\Lambda$ be the additive subgroup of $M_2(E_v)$ generated by the matrices $(x_i)^{(l \mapsto l \otimes a)}$ for $i \in \kappa$ and $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$, and let $M$ be the additive subgroup generated by those $X \in D_v$ whose determinant has the form $1 \otimes a$ with $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$. Then, with $G = \big(\mathrm{Tr}_{L/K}(\mathrm{tr}(x_i x_j))\big)_{i,j \in \kappa}$ and all indices understood as the relative indices $[M : M \cap \Lambda]$ and $[\Lambda : M \cap \Lambda]$ cast to $\mathbb{R}$,
--   $$\mathrm{N}(v)^2 \cdot [M : M \cap \Lambda]^2 \cdot \big\| \det G \big\|_v = \|16\|_v \cdot [\Lambda : M \cap \Lambda]^2,$$
--   where $\mathrm{N}(v)$ is the absolute norm of the ideal $v$, $\det G$ is viewed in $K_v$ through $K \to K_v$, and $\|\cdot\|_v$ is the norm on $K_v$.
--
--   At a place $v$ where the quadratically twisted commutant $D_v$ is a division algebra, the additive group $M$ is the unique maximal $\mathcal{O}_v$-order $\{X \in D_v : \mathrm{nrd}\,X \in \mathcal{O}_v\}$, and the identity compares it with the reference lattice spanned by the global basis $x$: the generalised index $[M:\Lambda]$ equals $\mathrm{N}(v)^{-1}\|{\det G}/16\|_v^{-1/2}$, the factor $\mathrm{N}(v)$ reflecting the reduced discriminant of a ramified quaternion algebra. It feeds the local integral computation [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar).
